# FIRE BLAST: a mage fireball's impact (mageFireball.pre FireImpact; GameProjectileComponent::destroy emits two puffs
# through ParticleSystem::emitPuff, on every role, with fire_flash.pfx): orange embers thrown out low over the ground (the
# splash: ~2 m), rising a little as they cool. A puff plays the FIRST emitter only. `Rate` 0 and `Burst` = the puff's
# particle count. Colors are linear HDR (rgb * intensity); the scene tonemaps, so bright additive values glow.
ParticleEffect FireBlast
	Emitter Embers
		Texture Textures/Particles/spark.dds
		Rate 0
		Burst 22
		SpawnRadius 0.25
		Offset 0, 0.2, 0
		ConeAngle 170
		Speed 2.5 6.0
		Life 0.3 0.7
		Gravity 3.0
		Drag 2.5
		Turbulence 1.5 1.0 0.5
		Size 0.3 0.06
		SizeVariance 0.5
		VelocityStretch 0.04
		ColorStart 40.0, 14.0, 3.0, 1
		ColorEnd 6.0, 1.2, 0.2, 0
		Additivity 1
		FadeIn 0.01
		FadeOutStart 0.35
		SoftFade 0.1
